==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1615. From {{etyl|fr}} {{term|somnolent|somnolent|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|sompolent|sompolent|lang=fro}}, subsequently from {{etyl|la}} {{term|somnolentus|somnolentus|lang=la}}, {{etyl|la}} {{term|somnus|somnus|sleep|lang=la}}, {{proto|Indo-European|swépnos||súpnos|dream}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈsɒmnələnt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈsɑːmnələnt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-somnolent.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[drowsy|Drowsy]] or [[sleepy]].
# {{dated}} Causing literal or figurative  sleepiness; [[soporific]].

